  "notes": "Brooklyn drill over the 808Melo grammar. Skippy displaced snares and rims, a kick that avoids the grid, triplet hat stutters and woodblock percs, under gliding portamento 808s that carry the melody across bar-lines. ⚠ **A register here spanned less than an octave and has been widened.** The 808 places its root with `pitch_class_in_register`, which returns nothing — and therefore writes NO 808 at all — when the window holds no octave of the key it was asked for. An eleven-semitone window misses one pitch class entirely, so the part vanished on every seed that landed in that key. The centre of the authored range is unchanged.",
